<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ debt markets closed on Wednesday, Thursday.</title>
<headline>NZ debt markets closed on Wednesday, Thursday.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-01-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Zealand debt markets were closed on Wednesday and Thursday for the New Year's break, with trade resuming on Friday, January 3.</p>
<p>At Tuesday's close the 90-days were at 7.90 percent, while the 02/00 bond was four points weaker at 7.01 percent and the 10-year maturity was a point weaker at 7.20 percent.</p>
<p>-- Wellington Newsroom (64 4) 473 4746</p>
</text>
